lesson: 212
title: Pairs and odd socks
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A pair is two things that go together: a pair of socks is 2 socks, a pair of shoes is 2 shoes.
explain: To count the single things, count 2 for every pair and then add the odd ones that have no partner.
explain: 6 pairs of socks and 3 odd socks: 6 × 2 = 12, and 12 + 3 = 15 socks.
vars: a=name p=2..12 k=2..5 z=2..9
answer: p * 2 + k
exercise: {a}'s drawer has {p} pairs of socks and {k} odd socks. How many socks are in the drawer?
exercise: There are {p} pairs of shoes in the hall and {k} shoes without a partner. How many shoes are there?
exercise: A jewellery box holds {p} pairs of earrings and {k} single earrings. How many earrings are in the box?
exercise: {a} packs {p} pairs of socks and {k} more socks that do not match anything. How many socks does {a.he} pack?
exercise: The lost-property box has {p} pairs of gloves and {k} single gloves. How many gloves are in it?
exercise: {p} pairs of socks on the line and {k} odd ones. how many socks
exercise: sock drawer: {p} pairs n {k} odd ones bc the washing machine eats them lol. how many socks total
exercise: {a} found {p+1} pairs, sorry {p} pairs and {k} odd socks under the bed. how many socks is that
exercise: my brother says {p} pairs is {p} socks. nope. {p} pairs plus {k} odd socks, how many socks
exercise: hall's a mess, {p+1} pairs of shoes — no wait, {p} pairs — and {k} on their own. how many shoes
exercise: {z} coats on the hooks and {p} pairs of trainers plus {k} single trainers on the floor. how many trainers
test: How many socks does {a} have if {a.he} owns {p} pairs and {k} socks with no partner?
test: Under the bed there are {k} lonely shoes and {p} complete pairs. Count the shoes.
test: In the shop window hang {p} pairs of earrings, and next to them {k} single ones. What is the number of earrings?
test: {k} odd socks plus {p} pairs, how many socks
test: grandma knitted me {p} pairs of socks and {k} extra 1s she didn't finish the partner for. socks total?
test: The changing room has {z} benches, {p} pairs of football boots and {k} boots on their own. How many boots are there?
exam: A drawer is found to contain {p} complete pairs of socks together with {k} unmatched socks. Determine the total number of individual socks therein.
exam: Given that a consignment comprises {p.words} pairs of shoes and {k.words} single shoes, ascertain the aggregate number of shoes.
exam: Compute the number of earrings held in a container in which {p} pairs and {k} solitary earrings are deposited.
exam: It is recorded that the lost-property office holds {p} pairs of gloves and, in addition thereto, {k} unpaired gloves. State the total number of gloves.
exercise: Grandpa's drawer had {p+1} pairs of socks and {k} odd socks. Since he passed on, Gran keeps one pair to remember him and gives all the rest to the charity shop. How many socks go to the shop?
exercise: bloody dog left a present on one pair of my socks, that pair's binned. had {p+1} pairs plus {k} odd ones. how many socks now
test: {a} told Mum there were "just a few" socks under the bed. That was a white lie: there were {p} pairs and {k} odd socks. How many socks were really under the bed?
